From f379139cfea07be2b460ba129cc111668ba4c198 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:57:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 33/34] ga2: IOP two-tier memory pool, CDVD stream HLE
 (sceCdRE, stm callbacks), SPU2 AutoDMA

- IOP heap: relocatable modules come from a low pool at 0x10000 before the
  main heap, so CDVDSTM/LIBSD buffers fit; allocation failures dump the map
  under GA2_IOP_ALLOC_TRACE.
- cdvdman: sceCdSC/Nop/RE/stm0Cb/stm1Cb/Break imports; stream-flagged reads
  complete through the registered stream callback.
- SPU2: AutoDMA (ADMA) with split-stereo input consumption, completion
  interrupts and restart/stop handling; ADMA writes no longer fault.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
